          "id": "SP_TESTACELLA_HALIOTIDEA_DRAPARNAUD_1801",
          "name": "Testacella haliotidea Draparnaud, 1801",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Testacella",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Gray-yellow body; shell 7 x 5 mm with brown periostracum; origins of dorsal grooves at the shell anterior are barely separated; not strong dorsal tubercles; pale sole and foot fringe (Quick 1960). </p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Strong lateral retractor muscles on buccal bulb; penis has a flagellum and apical caecum; penial flagellum is 2/3 length of penis; penial retractor begins at the diaphragm at the posterior end of the body; short, wide spermatheca duct (Quick 1960).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Has a smaller shell and thinner posterior than <em>T. maugei</em> (Quick 1960).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Eggs - 7 x 4 mm (Quick 1960).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:5190912"
